<title>UK: Deutsche Bank unit sets $250 mln Dec 1999 bond.</title>
<headline>Deutsche Bank unit sets $250 mln Dec 1999 bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by lead manager Deutsche Morgan Grenfell.</p>
<p> BORROWER   DEUTSCHE BANK FINANCE</p>
<p> GUARANTOR  DEUTSCHE BANK AG</p>
<p> AMT    $250 MLN	COUPON     6.50	MATURITY    29.DEC.99</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  100.975   PAY DATE   S29.APR.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.375     REOFFER    99.75     SPREAD	+10 BP</p>
<p> NOTES	S-SHORT FIRST COUPON</p>
<p> MOODY	AA1	 LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    =</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AAA	 DENOMS (K) 1-10-100  SALE LIMITS</p>
<p> US/UK/NA/DE</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    GERMAN    HOME CTRY  =	   TAX PROVS   STANDARD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.15	SELL CONC  1.225     PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p> UNDERLYING GOVT BOND 6.25 PCT MAR 1999 U.S. TREASURY</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
